WEBVTT

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:09.980
This is a work of fiction based on research into the period in which it is set. The people,
 organization, laws, and names that appear in it have no relation to any in the real world.

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:53.380
Slated for demolition, huh?

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:03.310
Everyone's disappearing.

00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:20.290
Sono, Yoh, you seem happy.

00:02:20.290 --> 00:02:22.000
We're only pretending.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:23.040
Huh?

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:26.750
Why aren't we allowed to go out?

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:29.250
You're safer with Mr. Tenmanya.

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:30.630
I know.

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:34.260
But I'm sick of playing house.

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:35.550
Did you find them?

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:36.550
Huh?

00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:38.510
Aren't you "it"?

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:41.010
Are you playing hide and seek?

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:46.440
Yeah, but I haven't managed to find anyone yet.

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:48.650
Have you asked Ayame?

00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:49.650
Huh?

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:52.740
Ayame knows lots of stuff.

00:02:55.030 --> 00:02:56.740
Your friends, mister?

00:02:56.740 --> 00:02:57.610
Yes.

00:02:57.610 --> 00:03:00.990
Do you know any people who fight vampires?

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:04.370
Anything at all.

00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:09.880
It's not a very nice rumor.

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:11.170
That's fine.

00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:13.960
Would you tell me?

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:17.380
They say someone is killing child vampires.

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:18.800
Huh?

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:23.640
He wears a weird mask and
attacks with things like knives.

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:25.810
The red specs roaming around

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:31.940
and that rumor are what made me
run away from where I used to stay.

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:34.440
Even after I met Sono and Yoh,

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:39.740
I was so scared that the masked man
might come after me.

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:41.950
Where were you before?

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:44.240
Near Tsukishima Island.

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:52.540
Suspicion

00:03:56.260 --> 00:03:57.800
Head clerk.

00:03:57.800 --> 00:03:59.760
Yes, sir?

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:02.680
Have your seen the man from Code Zero?

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:06.100
He went out about an hour ago.

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:08.020
If you need him, I could...

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:09.230
No, that's fine.

00:04:09.230 --> 00:04:11.440
It's not urgent.

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:13.110
I know.

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:16.280
He went to Tsukishima.

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:17.610
The island?

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:18.700
Hide and seek.

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:20.610
Be quiet, Yoh.

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:22.990
I think he was looking for someone.

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:33.210
I'm sure that they could find him
right away if they wanted to.

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:36.670
But, well, these are dangerous times.

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:54.570
This looks bad.

00:04:54.570 --> 00:04:56.230
Now I can't leave.

00:05:01.910 --> 00:05:04.490
So, those are the infamous red specs.

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:16.040
Be a good boy for me tonight, Danny Boy.

00:05:32.190 --> 00:05:37.150
Whoops. Looks like unexpected prey
stumbled into our net again.

00:05:37.150 --> 00:05:41.570
Once your work is done,
return home before morning.

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:52.210
That's Code Zero's base.

00:05:52.210 --> 00:05:55.500
The vampire units... aren't here.

00:06:18.070 --> 00:06:21.570
Suwa, it's Kurusu.

00:06:21.570 --> 00:06:23.450
Are you here?

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:41.210
I would look closer at him.

00:06:41.210 --> 00:06:45.220
I must look at him closer.

00:06:45.220 --> 00:06:50.430
I am Salomé, daughter of Herodias,
Princess of Judea.

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:54.560
Speak again, Jokanaan.

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:09.830
"<i>Salomé</i>"?

00:07:11.870 --> 00:07:14.710
This is Colonel Maeda, Special Forces Unit 16.

00:07:14.710 --> 00:07:15.870
Mr. Maeda?!

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:20.920
Suwa, Takeuchi, eliminate all vampires
that could become our enemies.

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:25.420
Artificial vampires, of course,
but larval vampires are also a threat.

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:27.720
Show them no mercy.

00:07:27.720 --> 00:07:30.850
"Larval"? Child vampires, too?

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:34.100
Shutaro Kurusu is also a risk factor.

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:36.560
If found, eliminate him immediately.

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:40.400
I repeat: eliminate Shutaro Kurusu.

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:43.110
I pray for your good fortune.

00:07:46.450 --> 00:07:49.780
Mr. Maeda! Where are you?!

00:07:50.990 --> 00:07:53.410
What's wrong with me?!

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:54.540
Mr. Maeda!

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:57.040
If you're here, come out!

00:08:02.670 --> 00:08:04.090
Where...?

00:08:14.310 --> 00:08:15.770
Suwa!

00:08:19.390 --> 00:08:22.860
Kurusu. You survived?

00:08:33.830 --> 00:08:36.950
Suwa... why?

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:42.540
Why?

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:46.550
They say someone is killing child vampires.

00:08:46.550 --> 00:08:47.970
Why?!

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:13.200
Oh, this is a real mess.

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:15.120
Well now...

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:28.010
Th-This is...

00:09:28.010 --> 00:09:30.130
R-Rotten fish?

00:09:32.050 --> 00:09:34.260
What do you think of my skunk balls?

00:09:34.260 --> 00:09:37.930
Great against vampires, aren't they?

00:09:37.930 --> 00:09:41.810
Takeuchi! What in hell do you think you're...

00:09:43.230 --> 00:09:46.980
What are you two fighting for?
We're on the same side.

00:09:46.980 --> 00:09:50.440
What do you mean?
Aren't you here to eliminate me?

00:09:50.440 --> 00:09:53.700
Oh, so you heard that.

00:09:53.700 --> 00:09:58.200
We're all troublemakers who got
kicked out of Special Forces Unit 16.

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:00.330
You fell for a trap like that?

00:10:00.330 --> 00:10:04.370
You're really not cut out
for soldiering, Kurusu.

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:06.750
What trap?

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:10.340
Maeda never prays for good fortune.

00:10:10.340 --> 00:10:12.380
You're to blame, too, Suwa.

00:10:12.380 --> 00:10:16.850
You're the oldest, so you ought
to be better at handling these things.

00:10:18.260 --> 00:10:23.480
The night's almost over, so the
vampire units will be coming back.

00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:30.280
I got what I could,
so let's move somewhere safe.

00:10:33.150 --> 00:10:36.530
Can I... trust this?

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:39.030
Trust what?

00:10:39.030 --> 00:10:41.620
Trust you two.

00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:45.540
That's for you to decide, not us.

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:49.670
Let's go, Suwa.

00:10:49.670 --> 00:10:50.750
Sure.

00:10:52.460 --> 00:10:53.590
Wait for me!

00:10:53.590 --> 00:10:55.050
I'm coming, too!

00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:07.860
Maeda...

00:11:07.860 --> 00:11:12.570
"Maeda never prays for good fortune."

00:11:12.570 --> 00:11:16.610
So, things just won't play out
like I hoped they would.

00:11:18.120 --> 00:11:22.120
And I even set the stage for them.

00:11:22.120 --> 00:11:24.830
Now to mop up.

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:28.920
Ltg. Nakajima likes things tidy.

00:11:28.920 --> 00:11:31.250
♪ Danny Boy... ♪

00:11:31.250 --> 00:11:34.800
♪ La la la... ♪

00:11:48.480 --> 00:11:51.150
I still can't get rid of the smell.

00:11:51.150 --> 00:11:55.280
I added <i>natto </i>to help it cling better.

00:11:55.280 --> 00:11:57.910
Do that again, and you'll regret it.

00:11:57.910 --> 00:12:01.700
I think the smell down here
is pretty bad in its own right.

00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:03.740
Umm...

00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:04.950
Yes?

00:12:04.950 --> 00:12:09.000
What happened to you two after Yokohama?

00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:12.380
Things went well until we
caught up to the vampire units,

00:12:12.380 --> 00:12:14.630
but there were just too many of them.

00:12:14.630 --> 00:12:18.010
We were keeping an eye
on them when the quake hit.

00:12:18.010 --> 00:12:20.590
We were worried about Code Zero HQ, too,

00:12:20.590 --> 00:12:25.350
but we took advantage of the confusion
to hole up in my own safe house first.

00:12:25.350 --> 00:12:27.390
So, what about you?

00:12:27.390 --> 00:12:29.190
Where's Boss Yamagami?

00:12:32.270 --> 00:12:35.070
Dead, huh?

00:12:35.070 --> 00:12:37.360
What about Mr. Maeda?

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:39.740
I haven't seen him yet,

00:12:39.740 --> 00:12:42.490
but I think he's all right.

00:12:42.490 --> 00:12:47.000
Colonel Maeda brought Yamagami's
wife a memento of him.

00:12:47.000 --> 00:12:48.710
But that recording...

00:12:48.710 --> 00:12:51.580
That wasn't really Colonel Maeda, right?

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:53.920
It must have been an impersonator.

00:12:53.920 --> 00:12:57.380
The voice was a perfect match for his, though.

00:12:57.380 --> 00:12:59.260
Why would anyone do that?

00:12:59.260 --> 00:13:02.180
Now that the vampire units are complete,

00:13:02.180 --> 00:13:07.060
we old models must be a thorn in their side.

00:13:07.060 --> 00:13:09.230
That's just like that brat.

00:13:09.230 --> 00:13:12.600
We came to Tsukishima Island
to check on something,

00:13:12.600 --> 00:13:15.070
but why were you there, Kurusu?

00:13:17.110 --> 00:13:18.400
What?

00:13:19.700 --> 00:13:24.530
I heard that you were
killing child vampires, Suwa.

00:13:24.530 --> 00:13:26.740
So, that's it.

00:13:26.740 --> 00:13:30.160
I also killed children. I won't deny it.

00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:35.170
Let's go outside from here.

00:13:37.460 --> 00:13:41.260
The sun must be up by now.

00:13:41.260 --> 00:13:43.640
Here, want some of this?

00:13:43.640 --> 00:13:44.600
Huh?

00:13:44.600 --> 00:13:47.010
It's sunblock I made.

00:13:47.010 --> 00:13:49.390
It's pretty popular in department stores.

00:13:49.390 --> 00:13:51.230
I'll share it with you.

00:13:51.230 --> 00:13:54.730
First research and now
you're going into business?

00:13:54.730 --> 00:13:56.520
It lasts a whole three minutes!

00:13:56.520 --> 00:13:58.230
I'll give you a discount.

00:13:58.230 --> 00:14:00.280
I don't need that junk.

00:14:02.360 --> 00:14:04.870
Well then, we should...

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:11.290
...get going, too.

00:14:11.290 --> 00:14:12.540
Right.

00:14:21.720 --> 00:14:25.180
The sun is glaring down on us.

00:14:25.180 --> 00:14:26.930
Where do we run to?

00:14:26.930 --> 00:14:28.720
Good question...

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:30.850
How about Mr. Tenmanya?

00:14:30.850 --> 00:14:32.310
He's safe?

00:14:32.310 --> 00:14:33.690
He moved.

00:14:33.690 --> 00:14:35.020
The <i>torii </i>corridor?

00:14:35.020 --> 00:14:36.650
You know about it?

00:14:36.650 --> 00:14:39.650
Yes, we've been there many times.

00:14:39.650 --> 00:14:41.820
Right, Suwa?

00:14:41.820 --> 00:14:44.070
What's wrong?

00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:48.620
A child vampire?

00:14:48.620 --> 00:14:50.870
There are some here, too, then.

00:14:50.870 --> 00:14:52.910
From the vaccine?

00:14:52.910 --> 00:14:54.670
Probably.

00:14:59.710 --> 00:15:03.550
They taste awful, but they stave off starvation.

00:15:05.300 --> 00:15:06.470
No!

00:15:13.980 --> 00:15:16.480
Why did you stop me?

00:15:16.480 --> 00:15:20.270
We can't save all of them on our own.

00:15:23.110 --> 00:15:29.700
I've lived a mere 300 years longer
than you, so I'll tell you.

00:15:29.700 --> 00:15:34.540
Why are there so few child vampires?

00:15:34.540 --> 00:15:37.460
They can't survive.

00:15:37.460 --> 00:15:39.250
They can't be in the sun,

00:15:39.250 --> 00:15:41.000
they sink in water,

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:42.920
they can't stand smells,

00:15:42.920 --> 00:15:47.220
and they can't stay in one place
because they don't age.

00:15:47.220 --> 00:15:52.180
Living as a vampire is 100 times
harder than it is for humans.

00:15:59.940 --> 00:16:01.190
Welcome back.

00:16:01.190 --> 00:16:02.110
A child?

00:16:02.110 --> 00:16:04.070
These kids are fine.

00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:06.820
You found them?

00:16:06.820 --> 00:16:07.860
Yup.

00:16:07.860 --> 00:16:09.200
Oh!

00:16:09.200 --> 00:16:11.780
What have we here?

00:16:11.780 --> 00:16:15.040
Children who the vaccine turned into vampires.

00:16:15.040 --> 00:16:17.870
I got Tenmanya to take them in.

00:16:17.870 --> 00:16:20.080
Oh, gentlemen.

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:22.040
Welcome to our humble shop.

00:16:22.040 --> 00:16:24.340
It's been too long, head clerk.

00:16:24.340 --> 00:16:27.010
The young master is inside.

00:16:28.720 --> 00:16:30.720
What a rare find!

00:16:30.720 --> 00:16:34.770
Three child vampires who
kept their sanity at once!

00:16:34.770 --> 00:16:37.940
I can't believe that vaccine is so effective.

00:16:37.940 --> 00:16:39.900
I'm impressed.

00:16:39.900 --> 00:16:42.020
What's in that vaccine?

00:16:42.020 --> 00:16:47.900
Ltg. Nakajima must have manufactured it
in Akabane using what I was studying

00:16:47.900 --> 00:16:51.740
and the Ascra he Imported through Yokohama.

00:16:51.740 --> 00:16:53.830
That brat Nakajima...

00:16:56.120 --> 00:16:57.410
What's wrong?

00:16:57.410 --> 00:17:01.960
Isn't he the killer from the rumors?

00:17:01.960 --> 00:17:05.670
Don't worry. Suwa is a nice person.

00:17:05.670 --> 00:17:08.260
But... he scares me.

00:17:11.050 --> 00:17:14.390
What are you staring at my face for?

00:17:14.390 --> 00:17:15.680
I'm sorry.

00:17:15.680 --> 00:17:19.810
If you're Mr. Kurusu's friend,
you must be a good person.

00:17:19.810 --> 00:17:22.560
You decide if I'm good or not.

00:17:22.560 --> 00:17:23.940
Huh?

00:17:23.940 --> 00:17:26.150
It's your decision.

00:17:27.400 --> 00:17:28.440
Still...

00:17:28.440 --> 00:17:31.910
With so many vampires gathered here,

00:17:31.910 --> 00:17:35.030
supplying them with food must be tough.

00:17:35.030 --> 00:17:37.830
Exactly.

00:17:37.830 --> 00:17:40.710
Not only is nothing we do ever enough,

00:17:40.710 --> 00:17:44.540
but the number of vampires
is skyrocketing from that vaccine.

00:17:44.540 --> 00:17:48.670
It's Tenmanya's policy to never
refuse a request for aid.

00:17:48.670 --> 00:17:51.680
You'll have a riot on your hands at this rate.

00:17:51.680 --> 00:17:55.350
I want to move them all
somewhere so that won't happen.

00:17:55.350 --> 00:17:57.220
Do you have any leads?

00:17:57.220 --> 00:17:59.220
If rumors count.

00:17:59.220 --> 00:18:04.440
I hear there's a village of vampires
hidden in a quarry in this area.

00:18:04.440 --> 00:18:06.770
Ever heard of it, Suwa?

00:18:06.770 --> 00:18:08.400
Never.

00:18:08.400 --> 00:18:13.860
Well, since it's never been found out,
it must be quite a village.

00:18:13.860 --> 00:18:17.990
I'd like to have the head clerk
scout it out for me.

00:18:17.990 --> 00:18:19.200
I see.

00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:23.580
We have to prepare, so we'll
probably make the move in winter.

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:27.540
We'll have to make do until then, of course.

00:18:27.540 --> 00:18:32.090
If you need food, I do know
one place you might get it.

00:18:32.090 --> 00:18:33.470
Really?

00:18:33.470 --> 00:18:36.390
It should tide you over for now, at least.

00:18:36.390 --> 00:18:41.600
We'll have to get a little rough for it to work,

00:18:41.600 --> 00:18:44.100
but that should be no problem for these two.

00:18:44.100 --> 00:18:44.810
Huh?

00:18:44.810 --> 00:18:46.400
So, we have to do the work?

00:18:46.400 --> 00:18:49.650
Yes, I'm counting on you.

00:18:49.650 --> 00:18:51.110
What is it?

00:18:52.820 --> 00:18:53.950
Nothing.

00:18:55.410 --> 00:18:57.070
She's taken a dislike to you.

00:18:57.070 --> 00:18:59.080
She never liked me to begin with.

00:18:59.080 --> 00:19:02.700
Oh, come on, I know you're dying for affection.

00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:04.750
Shut up.

00:19:04.750 --> 00:19:07.630
The effectiveness of the vampire units

00:19:07.630 --> 00:19:11.420
is proven by their work maintaining
order after the earthquake.

00:19:11.420 --> 00:19:16.430
Doesn't this clear the way
for their official adoption?

00:19:16.430 --> 00:19:21.220
Your argument is sound, but we
have other concerns at present.

00:19:21.220 --> 00:19:24.690
The world's attention is focused on Tokyo.

00:19:24.690 --> 00:19:26.600
Maintaining order is important,

00:19:26.600 --> 00:19:31.900
but a speedy recovery is what will
prove that we're a developed nation.

00:19:31.900 --> 00:19:33.860
The government wants military cuts.

00:19:33.860 --> 00:19:37.740
They just sent us a directive
to focus all efforts on rebuilding.

00:19:37.740 --> 00:19:39.120
I see!

00:19:39.120 --> 00:19:40.080
Besides,

00:19:40.080 --> 00:19:44.870
I hear their heavy gear and glowing
red spectacles frighten civilians.

00:19:44.870 --> 00:19:50.920
What we need to recover now
is the people's trust, not military might.

00:19:50.920 --> 00:19:53.300
Aren't they a force that never tires?

00:19:53.300 --> 00:19:57.470
Maybe they'd be more
useful as military engineers.

00:19:57.470 --> 00:20:01.220
Exactly! They're a perfect fit.

00:20:01.220 --> 00:20:07.060
You won't waver in your decision to use
the vampire units for such a purpose?

00:20:08.690 --> 00:20:12.980
Oh, Nakajima, that's just
what the times call for.

00:20:12.980 --> 00:20:14.230
That's right.

00:20:14.230 --> 00:20:17.860
The men are working hard to demolish Ryounkaku.

00:20:17.860 --> 00:20:20.950
I don't care if they're vampires or van drivers;

00:20:20.950 --> 00:20:24.410
right now, we need all the help we can get.

00:20:24.410 --> 00:20:25.540
How about this?

00:20:25.540 --> 00:20:28.870
We'll leave the vampire issue in your hands,

00:20:28.870 --> 00:20:34.800
but we'll discuss officially adopting
the vampire units once Tokyo is restored.

00:20:34.800 --> 00:20:36.130
Understood?

00:20:48.270 --> 00:20:52.360
What do those pencil-pushers know?

00:20:55.360 --> 00:20:56.900
Come on, Danny Boy.

00:20:56.900 --> 00:20:59.150
It's dinner time.

00:20:59.150 --> 00:21:01.280
When fall turns to winter,

00:21:01.280 --> 00:21:04.580
that will be your time to shine.

00:21:16.050 --> 00:21:20.840
It's daytime, but you've got the curtains shut.

00:21:20.840 --> 00:21:22.260
Stop.

00:21:24.680 --> 00:21:27.600
Oh, Defrott, you're awake?

00:21:27.600 --> 00:21:30.690
I haven't been able to sleep
much since the quake.

00:21:30.690 --> 00:21:33.650
Don't interrupt me when I'm trying to rest.

00:21:33.650 --> 00:21:37.280
But I think you should
go out while it's still light.

00:21:37.280 --> 00:21:40.740
